{"name":"Vestige","hex":"#937899","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vestige","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mark left on the earth by a foot.","A faint mark or visible sign left by something which is lost, or has perished, or is no longer present."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vestige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vestige (restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"Vestige is a restaurant in Ocean Springs, Mississippi. It was a semifinalist in the Outstanding Restaurant category of the James Beard Foundation Awards in 2024."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vestige_(restaurant)","wikidata":"Q124474670"},{"title":"Vestigiality","blocks":[{"text":"Vestigiality is the retention, during the process of evolution, of genetically determined structures or attributes that have lost some or all of the ancestral function in a given species. Assessment of the vestigiality must generally rely on comparison with homologous features in related species. The emergence of vestigiality occurs by normal evolutionary processes, typically by loss of function of a feature that is no longer subject to positive selection pressures when it loses its value in a changing environment. The feature may be selected against more urgently when its function becomes definitively harmful, but if the lack of the feature provides no advantage, and its presence provides no disadvantage, the feature may not be phased out by natural selection and persist across species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Gray536.png/330px-Gray536.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vestigiality","wikidata":"Q627214"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Darwin-s-tubercle.jpg/500px-Darwin-s-tubercle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/